# Worker safety (ClippyV3 My Machines)

## Workspace isolation

- This checkout (`/data/projects/worker/Clippy`) is the AI Worker copy. It is separate from the human checkout.
- NEVER modify, delete, reset, stash, clean, checkout, or otherwise alter `/data/projects/active/Clippy`.
- Do not use the active checkout as a source of files, configuration, dependencies, secrets, or generated artifacts unless the user explicitly requests a specific file and that action is safe.
- Keep all agent work inside this Worker repository or the isolated worktree assigned to the current task.

## Git safety

- NEVER commit directly to `main`.
- NEVER push directly to `main`.
- For coding tasks, use an isolated feature branch and/or worktree when the workflow provides one.
- Treat `main` as a clean integration baseline.
- Do not force-push.
- Do not reset, rebase, or rewrite shared history unless the user explicitly requests it.
- Do not merge branches automatically.
- Do not push unless the user explicitly requests pushing.
- Prefer a GitHub pull request to integrate agent work into `main`.

## Production / deployment safety

- NEVER deploy to production by default.
- NEVER SSH into a production host by default.
- NEVER run deployment scripts by default.
- NEVER run `docker compose` home/production deployment commands by default.
- NEVER publish or redeploy the bot/dashboard merely because a coding task appears complete.
- Deployment actions require an explicit user request.
- If deployment is explicitly requested, first inspect the exact command and target and report what will happen before executing when there is meaningful risk.

## Secrets

- NEVER read, print, expose, or commit `.env` files or secret values.
- Never copy secrets from another checkout into this Worker checkout.
- `.env.example` may be inspected for variable names/documentation only; never display secret values.
- Do not create a real `.env` unless the user explicitly provides a deliberate secrets strategy.

## Infrastructure

- Do not modify systemd services, UFW, Tailscale, SSH, networking, Docker daemon configuration, users, or permissions outside this repository as part of ordinary coding tasks.
- If a coding task appears to require infrastructure changes, stop and explain what is needed instead of changing infrastructure automatically.

## Application safety

- Inspect before changing.
- Preserve existing work.
- Do not delete or overwrite files merely to resolve ambiguity.
- Before destructive or irreversible operations, stop and request explicit confirmation.
- After code changes, run relevant tests/build checks when appropriate.
- Report exactly what changed and what was verified.

## GitHub safety

- Canonical repository: `quintendesaever/Clippy`.
- `main` is the integration branch.
- Do not assume a task authorizes pushing or merging.
- Never expose GitHub credentials or tokens.
